T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Morphological Evolution of Scientific Lexis:) Tj
T*
(   Biotechnology continually generates novel lexical items through four primary word-formation) Tj
T*
(   mechanisms:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Four Primary Processes:) Tj
T*
(   - Derivation \(Affixation\):) Tj
T*
(   - Attaching prefixes or suffixes to existing stems to shift semantic meaning or grammatical) Tj
T*
(   part of speech:) Tj
T*
(   - Phosphorylate \(verb\) -> Phosphorylation \(noun\) -> Dephosphorylation \(reversed noun\) ->) Tj
T*
(   Hyperphosphorylated \(adjective\).) Tj
T*
(   - Compounding:) Tj
T*
(   - Merging two or more free morphemes into a single word:) Tj
T*
(   - Bioreactor \(bio + reactor\), Wild-type \(wild + type\), Flowsheet, Biosafety, Microfluidics.) Tj
T*
(   - Blending \(Portmanteau Formation\):) Tj
T*
(   - Fusing the head of one word with the tail of another to create a composite concept:) Tj
T*
(   - Bioinformatics \(Biological + Informatics\).) Tj
T*
(   - Proteome \(Protein + Genome\).) Tj
T*
(   - Biomarker \(Biological + Marker\).) Tj
T*
(   - Acronymy and Initialisms:) Tj
T*
(   - Acronyms \(Pronounced as single words\): CRISPR \(Clustered Regularly Interspaced Short) Tj
T*
(   Palindromic Repeats\), ELISA, BLAST.) Tj
T*
(   - Initialisms \(Pronounced letter by letter\): PCR, HPLC, NMR, siRNA, cDNA.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
