(   [Problem Statement]: Contrast 'discrete' versus 'discreet' and 'continuous' versus 'continual' in bioprocess engineering.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. 'Discrete' versus 'Discreet':) Tj
T*
(   - Discrete \(Spelled with 't' separating the two 'e's - Individually separate, distinct,) Tj
T*
(   non-continuous\):) Tj
T*
(   - "The algorithm analyzed fifty discrete genomic loci.") Tj
T*
(   - "Bioreactor feed was delivered in discrete aliquots rather than an uninterrupted stream.") Tj
T*
(   - Memory Hook: The two 'e's are separated by the 't', mirroring separation into distinct units.) Tj
T*
(   - Discreet \(Spelled with two adjacent 'e's together - Prudent, secretive, circumspect\):) Tj
T*
(   - "The bioethics committee conducted discreet interviews with trial subjects.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. 'Continuous' versus 'Continual':) Tj
T*
(   - Continuous \(Unbroken, uninterrupted temporal or spatial progression without pause\):) Tj
T*
(   - "The continuous-flow centrifuge operated without interruption for 48 hours.") Tj
T*
(   - "A continuous linear gradient was generated.") Tj
T*
(   - Continual \(Recurring repeatedly at regular or intermittent intervals, with pauses between\):) Tj
T*
(   - "The fermentation vessel suffered continual pressure spikes throughout the night.") Tj
T*
(   - "Continual maintenance is required to prevent biofilm accumulation.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
